{"id":"H3093","lemma":"יָהִיר","transliteration":"yahir","sayIt":"YA-hir","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"adjective","gloss":"proud","meaning":"proud, arrogant, haughty","glosses":["arrogant man","arrogant"],"count":2,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"pro-21","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"and arrogant man","kjv":"and haughty"}},{"chapterId":"hab-2","v":5,"renderings":{"bsb":"He is an arrogant","kjv":"he is a proud"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Proverbs 21:24","note":"The proud and arrogant man—“Scoffer” is his name— he works in the arrogance of pride.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Habakkuk 2:5","note":"Yes, moreover, wine is treacherous. An arrogant man who doesn’t stay at home, who enlarges his desire as Sheol, and he is like death, and can’t be satisfied…","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}